WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.880
Will Ferrell and John C. Reilly are one of
the most dynamic comedy duos in Hollywood,

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.400
having previously joined forces to split sides
in Step Brothers and Talladega Nights: The

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.580
Ballad of Ricky Bobby.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.480
"Don't you stick that knife in your leg!"

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.720
But sadly, Ferrell and Reilly's latest venture,
the Sherlock Holmes spoof Holmes &amp; Watson,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.840
looks like a total bust.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.100
Professional critics and a horde of Twitter
randos alike say the film is so bad that some

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.320
audience members are leaving theaters before
the credits roll, with some even requesting

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:35.920
refunds.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.100
Directed by Tropic Thunder and Idiocracy co-writer
Etan Cohen, Holmes &amp; Watson opened on Christmas

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.340
Day 2018, but wasn't screened to members of
the media ahead of its wide launch.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.160
Once critics and fans actually feasted their
eyes upon what ought to have been another

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.660
hilarious Ferrell-Reilly two-hander, things
went sour fast.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.319
As of the making of this video, Holmes &amp; Watson
sits at a bleak five percent critical approval

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.680
rating and 26 percent fan score on Rotten
Tomatoes.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.440
One viewer wrote bluntly on Twitter,

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.280
"Holmes and Watson was the worst f---ing movie
of all time.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.200
First movie I've ever walked out on."

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:07.900
'What?

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.040
Were you saying something?"

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.560
Another random enraged moviegoer tweeted,

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.280
"@HolmesAndWatson is an absolute disaster.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.790
Had to wake up 3 other family members 40 minutes
in just to walk out.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:20.860
Possibly overtakes Ishtar as worse movie of
all time!

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.720
Don't waste your $ or time!"

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:23.980
"That doesn’t make sense.”

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.179
1987's Ishtar, starring Warren Beatty and
Dustin Hoffman, is widely considered to be

00:01:29.179 --> 00:01:33.950
one of the worst cinematic disasters ever,
with Roger Ebert calling it at the time, quote,

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.740
"a lifeless, massive, lumbering exercise in
failed comedy."

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:38.560
"Do it!”

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:45.920
“AYE AYE YEE AYE AYE"

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.020
So, not exactly great company!

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.280
Bailing on a flick forty minutes in is pretty
bad.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.659
But it gets worse: A woman shared that she
and her boyfriend ...

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.780
"...walked out of Holmes and Watson 15 minutes
in.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.560
Boyfriend's movie choosing privileges are
cancelled."

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:00.700
Yikes!

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.080
So what went wrong?

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:07.039
On paper, Holmes &amp; Watson has everything going
for it: Ferrell and Reilly playing goofy versions

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:11.290
of Arthur Conan Doyle's classic characters,
a talented screenwriter sitting in the director's

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.940
seat, and a first-rate UK cast, including
Ralph Fiennes.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.340
In practice, however, nothing really worked.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:22.519
Critics have set aflame just about every aspect
of Holmes &amp; Watson, denouncing the lazy and

00:02:22.519 --> 00:02:26.900
out-of-control direction, the unfunny script
that misses the mark as a parody, and all

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.840
the heavy-handed references and jokes that
completely fall flat.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.220
In his review, Newsday's Rafer Guzmán described
Holmes &amp; Watson as,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.410
"[...] one of those movies that goes beyond
unfunny and into a comedy-cubist zone, where

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:42.440
jokes are no longer recognizable and laughter
is philosophically impossible."

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.600
Noel Murray of the Los Angeles Times was a
bit nicer, calling the film,

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:50.100
"[...] more of a well-meaning misfire than
a total train wreck, [...] frustrating mainly

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.520
because all of these folks can do much better."

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:56.459
Murray added that many of the actors looked,
quote, "befuddled about what they're supposed

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.620
to be doing," which is never a good sign.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:04.189
Peter Sobczynski from RogerEbert.com was far
more brutal in his half-star review, writing,

00:03:04.189 --> 00:03:08.470
"Holmes &amp; Watson is so excruciatingly awful
that you have to wonder what it was, other

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:12.189
than their paychecks, that could have possessed
the cast and crew to keep coming back each

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:15.560
day, when it must have been obvious from the
first day of shooting that the project was

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.540
the most hopeless of cases imaginable."

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:22.360
So, if you're looking for a laugh, the answer
appears elementary: avoid Holmes &amp; Watson

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:23.080
at all costs.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.220
"Yeah, no s--- Sherlock!"

